-- title:
--   Level automorphisms for Γ₀(M') form a finite subgroup
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_0:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota_0(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(X)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field attached to $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. The assertion is that there exists a finite subgroup $G$ of the group of $L$-algebra automorphisms of $K$ such that an automorphism $\tau$ lies in $G$ precisely when [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) holds for $\tau$ and $\gamma^{-1}$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$: that is, for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ with $p_g\neq 0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x)\cdot (g\mid_k \gamma^{-1,\sharp}) = (f\mid_k\gamma^{-1,\sharp})$ as $q$-expansions, where $\gamma^{-1,\sharp}$ denotes the conjugate $\binom{a\ \ b/(q\ell)}{(q\ell)c\ \ \ d}$ of $\gamma^{-1}=\binom{a\ b}{c\ d}$.
--
--   The automorphisms characterised here are the deck transformations of the covering of modular curves $X(\Gamma(q\ell)\cap\Gamma_0(M'))\to X_0(M')$, realised on the $q$-expansion model $K$ of the function field; the statement records that they form a single finite subgroup of $\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$. It supplies the finite group needed for the fixed-field (Artin) arguments about valuations and invariants on $K$ used in the full-level construction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_finite_subgroup_forall_mem_iff_exists_isLevelAutAt_of_exists_ringHom.lean

